Do not implement uncontrolled autonomous phone actions.
41. AI COMMUNICATION POLICY
Create configurable rules:

* which channels AI can use
* which customers can receive AI messages
* allowed hours
* message limits
* approval requirements
* prohibited content
* escalation conditions

Support English, Hausa, and Arabic.
Support RTL.
42. AI LANGUAGE DETECTION
Automatically detect:

* English
* Hausa
* Arabic

Respond in the customer's preferred language where known.
Allow manual language selection.
Never translate financial amounts incorrectly.
Currency values must remain machine-generated from authoritative records.
43. AI MULTI-CURRENCY SAFETY
When discussing money:
AI must retrieve the actual transaction currency.
Never guess exchange rates.
If conversion is required, use the existing currency service or approved exchange-rate source.
Clearly distinguish:

* original amount
* converted amount
* exchange rate
* date of rate

44. AGENT BUDGET CONTROL
Create AI usage limits.
Track:

* tokens
* requests
* estimated cost
* provider
* model
* tenant
* agent
* user

Support:

* daily limits
* monthly limits
* per-agent limits
* per-tenant limits
* emergency disable

45. MODEL ROUTING
Create model/provider abstraction.
Support:

* primary AI provider
* secondary provider
* local/mock provider

Allow routing based on:

* task
* cost
* latency
* capability

Do not hardcode the application to one AI provider.
46. AI FAILOVER
If an AI provider fails:

* retry safely
* use fallback provider if configured
* use deterministic workflow where possible
* notify user if necessary

Never duplicate financial actions because an AI request timed out.
47. IDEMPOTENCY FOR AI ACTIONS
Every state-changing AI action must use idempotency.
Examples:

* create payment link
* create task
* send message
* create booking
* cancel booking
* create refund request

A repeated AI response must not create duplicate transactions.
48. AGENT EXECUTION RECORD
Create an agent execution record.
Track:

